  "note": "What goes with what. There is no purchase history to mine and no analytics, so this is hand-written knowledge of an Indian kitchen -- which for one shop's catalogue is better than anything a cold-start algorithm would produce, and it can be corrected by someone who knows the shop rather than retrained.",

  "howItWorks": "Two layers. `byProduct` is specific and scores 3: tea really does want sugar and biscuits. `byCategory` is a fallback and scores 1: anything in snacks suggests something from drinks. Scores add up across the whole basket, so milk AND tea together push sugar to the top. Anything already in the basket is dropped, and the best few are shown.",

